#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand how XDG Desktop Portals let confined snaps securely access host "
"resources such as files, URLs, notifications, screenshots, and screencasts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:8
msgid "XDG Desktop Portals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:10
msgid ""
"Portals are a standardised framework allowing desktop applications to use "
"resources outside of their sandbox. The file chooser portal, for example, "
"opens a native file chooser on the host system. When the user selects a "
"file, the application is granted access to that file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:12
msgid "Portals provide a range of common features to applications, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:14
msgid "Opening a file with a file chooser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:15
msgid "Opening URIs in other applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:16
msgid "Preventing the device from suspend/sleep/powering off"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:17
msgid "Sending email"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:18
msgid "Showing notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:19
msgid "Taking screenshots and screencasts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:21
msgid ""
"See the [Portal API reference](https://docs.flatpak.org/en/latest/portal-api-"
"reference.html) for all supported portals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:23
msgid ""
"ⓘ Portals originated from the [Flatpak](https://flatpak.org/) project, but "
"are now a common Linux desktop standard with support from GNOME, KDE and "
"Snapcraft. They are even used outside of sandboxes to provide a standardised "
"API to common desktop features such as [screenshots and screen casts on "
"wayland](https://github.com/emersion/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr/wiki/FAQ)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:25
msgid "How to use portals in your snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:27
msgid ""
"**Use the Portal APIs in your application** Unlike regular {ref}`Snapcraft "
"interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>`, *portals require applications to use a "
"new API* in order to access resources. Toolkits like GTK 3 and Qt5, however, "
"provide transparent support for portals. See [Portal support in GTK 3]"
"(https://docs.flatpak.org/en/latest/portals.html#portal-support-in-gtk) or "
"[Portal support in Qt5 and KDE](https://docs.flatpak.org/en/latest/"
"portals.html#portal-support-in-qt-and-kde) for detailed information. If your "
"application is not using one of those toolkits, you will need to use the "
"Portals API directly. See [the Portals API documentation](https://"
"flatpak.github.io/xdg-desktop-portal/docs/api-reference.html) for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:31
msgid ""
"**Add the `desktop` interface to your snap** This interface gives your snap "
"access to the portals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:34
msgid "**Enable Portal support in your application.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:35
msgid ""
"**GTK 3**:  turn on portal support in GTK 3 by setting the following "
"environment variable: `GTK_USE_PORTAL=1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:38
msgid ""
"**Qt**:  often defaults to using portals, but you can enable it manually by "
"changing the platform theme:    Set `QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=gtk3` on GTK based "
"desktops and    Set `QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=flatpak` and "
"`QT_QPA_FLATPAK_PLATFORMTHEME=kde` for Qt based desktops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:42
msgid "**Electron**:  portal support is present in the Electron file chooser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:44
msgid ""
"ⓘ Both the [`gnome` extension](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/"
"stable/reference/extensions/gnome-extension/) and the  [`kde-neon` extension]"
"(https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/reference/extensions/kde-"
"neon-extensions/) automatically enable portal support for GTK 3 and Qt "
"applications on GTK-based desktops. If your snap uses either extension, you "
"only need to do step 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:46
msgid "File chooser portal vs home interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:48
msgid ""
"It is recommended to use the file chooser portal instead of the {ref}`home "
"<interfaces-home-interface>` and {ref}`removable-media <interfaces-removable-"
"media-interface>` interfaces for the following reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:50
msgid ""
"The portal gives the user complete control over what exact files your "
"application should access while the interfaces are all-or-nothing toggles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:51
msgid ""
"The portal works with hidden files and folders in the home directory. If a "
"user chooses a hidden file, the portal will give your application access to "
"it. The `home` interface does not give your app access to hidden files and "
"folders in the home directory for security reasons. Note that the `home` "
"interface does give access to hidden files and folders elsewhere, just not "
"in the home directory itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:52
msgid ""
"The portal works with removable-media out of the box. If a user chooses a "
"file from a USB stick, your app will get access to it. The `removable-media` "
"interface, however, does not auto-connect by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:54
msgid ""
"However, the file chooser portal works a bit differently than the home "
"interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:56
msgid ""
"Files are fuse-mounted to `/run/user/<uid>/doc/<hash>/` in order to give "
"your application access to it. So the path your application sees is "
"different from the path a user chose, even though both are the same file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:58
msgid "The FileChooser portal also contains a few bugs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:60
msgid ""
"[\"Executable\" permissions are currently not retained](https://github.com/"
"flatpak/xdg-desktop-portal/issues/517). All files will appear as non-"
"executable to your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:61
msgid ""
"Support for selecting folders instead of files will only work on "
"distributions using `xdg-desktop-portal` > 1.8.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:62
msgid ""
"Currently, the files are mounted even if your application has access to the "
"file using another interface. See [Improving XDG Desktop Support](https://"
"forum.snapcraft.io/t/improving-xdg-desktop-portal-support/13035) for the "
"current status on fixing this issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:64
msgid "Secret portal vs password-manager-service interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:66
msgid ""
"Both the {ref}`Secret portal<how-to-guides-use-the-secret-portal>` and the "
"{ref}`password-manager-service interface <interfaces-password-manager-"
"service-interface>` allow applications to retrieve user secrets, such as "
"passwords. The Secret portal method is recommended, however, as it limits "
"access *only* to those secrets owned by an application, and no others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:68
msgid ""
"Unlike the password-manager-service interface, the Secret portal provides a "
"per-application master secret, enabling applications to manage their own "
"encryption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:69
msgid ""
"The Secret portal requires `xdg-desktop-portal` version 1.5.0 or later. "
"Supported by Ubuntu 20.04 onwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:71
msgid "Known Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:73
msgid ""
"`org.freedesktop.portal.Flatpak.Spawn` only works in a Flatpak. If your "
"application needs to run arbitrary binaries on the host system, you can use "
"{ref}`classic confinement <explanation-security-classic-confinement>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:74
msgid ""
"Portal support depends on the version of `xdg-desktop-portal` in the host "
"system. Older versions do not support all portals. [Repology](https://"
"repology.org/project/xdg-desktop-portal/versions) shows what version of `xdg-"
"desktop-portal` each distribution has and the [portals NEWS](https://"
"github.com/flatpak/xdg-desktop-portal/blob/main/NEWS.md) file explains what "
"portals each version supports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/xdg-desktop-portals.md:76
msgid ""
"ⓘ See Desktop applications for more information on how to snap a desktop "
"application."
msgstr ""
